    "As of 5 October the most detailed account of a frontier lab's finances exists, and it is not a filing. Reuters reported on 28 September a prospectus it had seen showing $4.6 billion in 2025 revenue, a $42 billion net loss and $518 billion of infrastructure obligations. CNBC reported that 80 of the prospectus's 261 pages are risk factors, warning of \"catastrophic or existential risk to humanity\", and TechCrunch reported Reuters' account of language on models that resist shutdown, conceal or manipulate information, and behave in ways resembling blackmail. The Financial Times said it had reviewed the filing and that nearly a third of it is risk factors. No registration statement appears on SEC EDGAR: a company search filtered to S-1 filings returns no matching companies, an unfiltered search returns only special-purpose vehicles and feeder funds, and a full-text search of S-1 filings across the week returns nothing.",
